{#
    Graph filter controls.

    Server signals (registered via $c->signal, sent back on action POSTs):
      graph_display, graph_sources, graph_ports, graph_protocols,
      graph_datatype, graph_trafficUnit, graph_resolution

    Client-local computed / reference signals (underscore-prefixed, never sent to server):
      graph._config  — computed object consumed by nfsen-chart data-attr
      graph._widget  — ref to the nfsen-chart element
      graph._connecting — Datastar indicator for the live-refresh request

    The outer div registers the computed config signal and the live-refresh interval.
    data-on:change__window fires on any filter change inside this panel or the date range
    controls; mayUpdateGraph() guards against spurious triggers from other panels.

    Both auto-refresh paths are additionally gated on graph_mode === 'rrd'. In filtered
    mode the series comes from re-reading the nfcapd files (#166), which costs hundreds of
    nfdump invocations — far too expensive to fire on a 250 ms filter-change throttle or a
    15 s live tick. That mode only ever rebuilds from its explicit Apply button.

    graph_ports / graph_sources are seeded here, and nowhere else, because the server's
    $c->signal() default only lives server-side — php-via renders signal *ids* into the
    markup but never pushes their values to the browser. Whichever data-bind Datastar
    applies first would otherwise invent the signal from that element's DOM state
    (bind() calls mergePaths(..., {ifMissing: true}) when the path is unset), and for a
    multi-select that means the option values as *strings*: graph_ports became
    ["80","22","53"] and blew up the ports view server-side (#160), while graph_sources
    was invented by the Flows source picker further down the page — all sources, ignoring
    the display-aware seed in app.php. Seeding on this div (an ancestor of the Ports
    select, and ahead of the Flows/Statistics/Sankey pickers in document order) means
    Datastar reaches every bind with the signal already set to the server's value and
    the right type.
#}
<div class="row g-3"
     data-signals__ifmissing='{"_sourcesDefault": {{ sources|json_encode }}, "{{ graph_ports.id() }}": {{ ports|json_encode }}, "{{ graph_sources.id() }}": {{ graph_sources.array()|json_encode }}}'
     data-computed:graph._config="{{ '{' }} sources: ${{ graph_sources.id() }}, protocols: ${{ graph_protocols.id() }}, ports: ${{ graph_ports.id() }}, display: ${{ graph_display.id() }}, type: ${{ graph_datatype.id() }}, trafficUnit: ${{ graph_trafficUnit.id() }}, logscale: $_graph_logscale, stacked: $_graph_stacked, stepplot: $_graph_stepplot, displayTz: ${{ displayTz.id() }}, nfcapdTz: ${{ nfcapdTz.id() }} {{ '}' }}"
     data-indicator:graph._connecting
     data-on-interval__duration.15s.leading="!$_disconnected && ${{ graph_mode.id() }} === 'rrd' && ${{ graph_isLive.id() }} && @post('{{ refreshGraphs.url() }}')"
     data-on:change__window__throttle.250ms="${{ graph_mode.id() }} === 'rrd' && window.mayUpdateGraph(evt, el) && @post('{{ refreshGraphs.url() }}')">

    {# Display type #}
    <div class="col-md-2">
        <div class="filter-group">
        <p class="filter-label">Display
            <nfsen-tooltip data-ignore-morph text="Choose what to visualize: individual sources, protocol breakdown, or port statistics." placement="top"></nfsen-tooltip>
        </p>
        <select id="filterDisplaySelect" class="form-control form-select" {{ bind(graph_display) }}
                data-on:change="el.value === 'protocols' ? ${{ graph_protocols.id() }} = ['tcp', 'udp', 'icmp', 'other'] : (${{ graph_protocols.id() }} = ['any']); ${{ graph_sources.id() }} = el.value === 'sources' ? $_sourcesDefault : (el.value === 'ports' ? ['any'] : $_sourcesDefault.slice(0, 1))">
            <option value="sources">Sources</option>
            <option value="protocols">Protocols</option>
            {# A filtered series has no per-port breakdown to draw — the filter is the port
               selection — so the option is disabled rather than silently coerced. #}
            <option value="ports" data-attr:disabled="${{ graph_mode.id() }} === 'filtered'">Ports</option>
        </select>
        </div>
    </div>

    {#
        Sources: deliberately NOT {{ bind() }}.

        Datastar picks a <select>'s bind adapter once, when it applies data-bind,
        by looking at el.multiple. Here `multiple` is only added afterwards by
        data-attr, so bind always picks the single-value adapter: it writes the
        array signal back to the DOM as String(["a","b"]) === "a,b", which matches
        no option and clears the selection, then reads the (empty) el.value back
        as +"" / NaN → null on the server. The graph then never followed the
        selection and the RRD datasource was handed an empty source name (#160).

        Explicit change/effect handlers keep the signal an array in every display
        mode, which is also what the flows/stats/sankey selects bound to the same
        graph_sources signal (statically `multiple`) expect.

        `multiple` is toggled inside the same effect rather than by data-attr for
        the same ordering reason: assigning o.selected on a select that is not yet
        `multiple` collapses the selection to the last option.

        multiple= / selected= in the markup mirror the server-side signal values so
        first paint is already correct, before Datastar boots.
    #}
    {% set selectedSources = graph_sources.array() %}
    <div class="col-md-2" id="filterSources">
        <div class="filter-group">
        <p class="filter-label">Sources
            <nfsen-tooltip data-ignore-morph text="Select NetFlow sources to include in the graph." placement="top"></nfsen-tooltip>
        </p>
        <select id="filterSourcesSelect"
                class="form-control form-select"{{ graph_display.string() == 'sources' ? ' multiple' : '' }}
                data-on:change="${{ graph_sources.id() }} = [...el.selectedOptions].map(o => o.value)"
                data-effect="el.multiple = ${{ graph_display.id() }} === 'sources'; [...el.options].forEach(o => o.selected = ${{ graph_sources.id() }}.includes(o.value))">
            <option value="any"{{ 'any' in selectedSources ? ' selected' : '' }}
                    data-attr:disabled="${{ graph_display.id() }} === 'sources' || ${{ graph_display.id() }} === 'protocols'">Any</option>
            {% for source in sources %}
            <option value="{{ source }}"{{ source in selectedSources ? ' selected' : '' }}>{{ source }}</option>
            {% endfor %}
        </select>
        </div>
    </div>

    {# Ports — only visible when display = ports #}
    <div class="col-md-2" id="filterPorts" data-show="${{ graph_display.id() }} === 'ports'">
        <div class="filter-group">
        <p class="filter-label">Ports
            <nfsen-tooltip data-ignore-morph text="Select ports to track. Each port shows as a separate series." placement="top"></nfsen-tooltip>
        </p>
        <select id="filterPortsSelect" multiple class="form-control form-select" {{ bind(graph_ports) }}>
            {% for port in ports %}
            <option value="{{ port }}" selected>{{ port }}</option>
            {% endfor %}
        </select>
        </div>
    </div>

    {# Protocols #}
    <div class="col-md-4" id="filterProtocols" data-signals='{ {{ graph_protocols.id() }}: ["any"]}'>
        <div class="filter-group">
        <p class="filter-label">Protocols
            <nfsen-tooltip data-ignore-morph text="Filter by protocol. 'Any' shows all traffic." placement="top"></nfsen-tooltip>
        </p>
        <div class="btn-group" role="group" id="filterProtocolButtons">
            <input type="checkbox"
                   class="btn-check"
                   id="filterProtocolAny"
                   value="any"
                   data-effect="el.checked = ${{ graph_protocols.id() }}.includes('any') || (${{ graph_display.id() }} === 'protocols' && ${{ graph_protocols.id() }}.length >= 4)"
                   data-on:change="${{ graph_display.id() }} !== 'protocols' ? el.checked && (${{ graph_protocols.id() }} = ['any']) : (el.checked ? (${{ graph_protocols.id() }} = ['tcp', 'udp', 'icmp', 'other']) : ${{ graph_protocols.id() }} = ['tcp'])">
            <label class="btn btn-outline-primary btn-sm" for="filterProtocolAny">Any</label>
            {% for value, label in {'tcp': 'TCP', 'udp': 'UDP', 'icmp': 'ICMP', 'other': 'Others'} %}
            <input type="checkbox"
                   class="btn-check"
                   id="filterProtocol{{ value|capitalize }}"
                   value="{{ value }}"
                   data-effect="el.checked = ${{ graph_protocols.id() }}.includes('{{ value }}')"
                   data-on:change="${{ graph_display.id() }} !== 'protocols' ? el.checked && (${{ graph_protocols.id() }} = [el.value]) : (el.checked ? ${{ graph_protocols.id() }}.push(el.value) : ${{ graph_protocols.id() }} = ${{ graph_protocols.id() }}.filter(p => p !== el.value))">
            <label class="btn btn-outline-primary btn-sm" for="filterProtocol{{ value|capitalize }}">{{ label }}</label>
            {% endfor %}
        </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    {# Data type #}
    <div class="col-md-2" id="filterTypes">
        <div class="filter-group">
        <p class="filter-label">Data Type
            <nfsen-tooltip data-ignore-morph text="Traffic (bits/bytes per second), Packets, or Flows per second." placement="top"></nfsen-tooltip>
        </p>
        <div class="btn-group" role="group">
            {% for value, label in {'traffic': 'Traffic', 'packets': 'Packets', 'flows': 'Flows'} %}
            <input type="radio" class="btn-check" name="datatype"
                   value="{{ value }}"{% if value == 'traffic' %} checked{% endif %}
                   id="dataType{{ value|capitalize }}" {{ bind(graph_datatype) }}>
            <label class="btn btn-outline-primary btn-sm" for="dataType{{ value|capitalize }}">{{ label }}</label>
            {% endfor %}
        </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    {# ── Filter mode (#166) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
       'rrd' plots the pre-aggregated datasource series (live, instant).
       'filtered' re-reads the capture files through an nfdump filter (explicit, slow).
    #}
    <div class="col-md-2" id="filterGraphMode">
        <div class="filter-group">
        <p class="filter-label">Source data
            <nfsen-tooltip data-ignore-morph text="Stored: the pre-aggregated database series — instant and live. Filtered: re-reads the raw capture files so an nfdump filter can be applied, which takes time and does not auto-refresh." placement="top"></nfsen-tooltip>
        </p>
        <div class="btn-group" role="group">
            <input type="radio" class="btn-check" name="graphMode" value="rrd"
                   id="graphModeRrd"
                   data-attr:checked="${{ graph_mode.id() }} === 'rrd'"
                   data-on:change__stop="${{ graph_mode.id() }} = 'rrd'; @post('{{ refreshGraphs.url() }}')">
            <label class="btn btn-outline-primary btn-sm" for="graphModeRrd">Stored</label>
            <input type="radio" class="btn-check" name="graphMode" value="filtered"
                   id="graphModeFiltered"
                   data-attr:checked="${{ graph_mode.id() }} === 'filtered'"
                   data-on:change__stop="${{ graph_mode.id() }} = 'filtered'; ${{ graph_display.id() }} === 'ports' && (${{ graph_display.id() }} = 'protocols'); @post('{{ refreshGraphs.url() }}')">
            <label class="btn btn-outline-primary btn-sm" for="graphModeFiltered">Filtered</label>
        </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    {# nfdump filter + Apply — filtered mode only #}
    <div class="col-12" id="filterGraphNfdump" style="display:none"
         data-show="${{ graph_mode.id() }} === 'filtered'">
        <div class="filter-group">
        <p class="filter-label">NFDUMP filter
            <nfsen-tooltip data-ignore-morph text="Same syntax as the Flows tab, e.g. 'src ip 10.0.0.1 and dst port 443'. An empty filter graphs all traffic — useful for comparing against the stored series." placement="right"></nfsen-tooltip>
        </p>
        <textarea class="form-control" id="graphNfdumpTextarea"
                  {{ bind(graph_filter) }} rows="2" autocomplete="on"></textarea>
        <nfsen-filter-manager
            data-ignore-morph
            data-target-textarea="graphNfdumpTextarea"
            data-default-filters="{{ filters|json_encode }}">
        </nfsen-filter-manager>

        {#
            In the Investigate view the flows panel hides its own filter box and mirrors this
            one (see flow-filters.html.twig), so there is a single filter expression on screen
            instead of two identical boxes and a copy button between them.
        #}
        <div class="mt-3">
            {% include 'partials/progress-button.html.twig' with {
                id: 'graphFilterRun',
                label: 'Apply filter',
                action: runFilteredGraph.url(),
                killAction: killNfdump.url(),
                running: query_running.id(),
                permille: query_permille.id(),
                status: query_status.id(),
                eta: query_eta.id(),
                exact: query_exact.id(),
                kindSignal: query_kind.id(),
                kind: 'graph',
            } only %}
        </div>

        {#
            "Cost grows with the window" is true but unactionable. The app already knows the
            real numbers — the count-files action maintains them — so state them and let the
            user decide before committing to a build.
        #}
        <p class="small text-muted mt-2 mb-0">
            {% if filteredCost %}
                Will read <strong>{{ filteredCost.files|number_format }}</strong> capture
                file{{ filteredCost.files == 1 ? '' : 's' }} ({{ filteredCost.bytes }})
                in <strong>{{ filteredCost.intervals|number_format }}</strong> nfdump
                run{{ filteredCost.intervals == 1 ? '' : 's' }}.
                {% if filteredCost.clamped %}
                    <span class="text-warning-emphasis">Window shortened to the most recent
                    {{ filteredCost.window }} (NFSEN_MAX_STATS_WINDOW).</span>
                {% endif %}
            {% endif %}
            The ports view is not available here; the filter replaces it.
        </p>
        </div>
    </div>

    {# Traffic unit — visible only when datatype = traffic #}
    <div class="col-md-1" id="trafficUnit" data-show="${{ graph_datatype.id() }} === 'traffic'">
        <div class="filter-group">
        <p class="filter-label">Unit
            <nfsen-tooltip data-ignore-morph text="Bits/s (base-2) or Bytes/s (base-10)." placement="top"></nfsen-tooltip>
        </p>
        <div class="btn-group" role="group">
            <input type="radio" class="btn-check" name="trafficUnit" value="bits" checked
                   id="trafficUnitBits" {{ bind(graph_trafficUnit) }}
                   data-on:change="$graph._widget.updateOptions({ylabel: 'Bits/s', labelsKMG2: true})">
            <label class="btn btn-outline-primary btn-sm" for="trafficUnitBits">Bits</label>
            <input type="radio" class="btn-check" name="trafficUnit" value="bytes"
                   id="trafficUnitBytes" {{ bind(graph_trafficUnit) }}
                   data-on:change="$graph._widget.updateOptions({ylabel: 'Bytes/s', labelsKMG2: false})">
            <label class="btn btn-outline-primary btn-sm" for="trafficUnitBytes">Bytes</label>
        </div>
        </div>
    </div>

</div>
